  "id": "generation-loop",
  "after": "overview",
  "title": "Writing is one guess, repeated.",
  "caption": "An LLM writes one token at a time. At each step it reads every token so far: your prompt plus what it already wrote. It adds one new token and starts again. It stops when it predicts a special end token or reaches a length limit (सीमा, seema). To keep it simple, each word is drawn as one token. In fact, the tokeniser of GPT-2 (an older OpenAI model) splits “wickets” into “w” and “ickets”.",
  "alt": "A loop: text so far goes into the GPT model, which predicts one next token that is added back to the text. Below, four rows grow from the prompt \"India won by\" to \"India won by 6 wickets.\" and finally an end token, one token per row.",
