  "title": "What to look for at 500 and 5,000 steps.",
  "caption": "The loss (the error number) starts near 4.17 for a model with 65 characters, because a blind guess has a 1 in 65 chance. As training goes on, the loss falls and the text improves: first spaces and short word shapes, then real words, names and line breaks. The curve and the two samples are made up, to show what to describe in your answer.",
  "alt": "A falling loss curve from about 4.17 at the start, with a yellow point at step 500 and a green point at step 5,000, where it is much lower. Below, two made-up samples: at step 500 \"Thes wo hat thou lorer, and mou\", mostly broken words; at step 5,000 \"ROMEO: What say you, my lord?\", real words and a name.",
